From: Wine Fox
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: A monitor with a single host mode is where its current mode is.

A display source whose host has one mode only took that mode for its physical one, with no
position: its monitor was at 0,0, over the primary one, whatever the position of the current
mode. Wayland compositors, KWin among them, give each output its current mode only, so on a
second monitor every monitor rect was wrong: windows maximized and menus placed against the
first monitor, and the work area was cut to nothing.

The physical mode now has the position of the current one.

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
index c9cc892..b853b9e 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -2226,6 +2226,9 @@ static void add_modes( const DEVMODEW *current, UINT host_modes_count, const DEV
     }
 
     physical = modes_count == 1 ? *modes : *current;
+    /* the host's only mode has no position: the monitor is where the current one is */
+    physical.dmFields |= current->dmFields & DM_POSITION;
+    physical.dmPosition = current->dmPosition;
     if (ctx->is_primary) ctx->primary = *current;
 
     detached.dmPelsWidth = 0;
